  <string name="ballrace_how_to_play">Physics</string>
  <string name="ballrace_physics_note">Balls fall under gravity with no air resistance. Collisions calculate rebound from both objects’ mass, velocity direction and restitution. Contact friction changes spin. Each ball uses the moment of inertia of a uniform solid disc. Balls finishing in the same simulation step are ranked by name. Balls have no outline. This 2D model is for game simulation, not precision engineering.</string>
